{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content \\\"D:\\\\Claude\\\\docs\\\\dispatch\\\\audit-conformance-s7s8-redispatch.md\\\" -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"# DISPATCH: Audit Conformance S7-S8 — Discovery Authority + Verification Exactness\n\n## 0. Dispatch Control\n\n- **Dispatch ID:** dispatch-audit-conformance-s7s8-20260805\n- **Requester:** Adrian\n- **Dispatcher:** Claude Code primary orchestrator on `/Volumes/D/claude`\n- **Executor:** implementation executor with local repository write access\n- **Mode:** IMPLEMENT — bounded local source edits plus updated conformance cases\n- **Execution host / OS:** macOS Darwin 25.5.0 workstation\n- **Working directory:** `/Volumes/D/claude`\n- **Repository / branch:** /Volumes/D/claude at `main`\n- **Baseline revision:** `7e4c1c17` (post S2-S6/S9-S11 commit)\n- **User authorization:** Close S7 and S8 only; commit, push, branch, worktree, network calls, dependency installs, & every other conformance item are forbidden.\n- **Integration owner:** Claude Code primary orchestrator reviews the diff and decides on commit.\n\n## 1. Mission\n\n- **Outcome:** Close the two remaining verified audit conformance gaps — discovery authority and verification exactness — with executable proof.\n- **Definition of done:** Both fixes exist in source; the updated conformance cases exit 0; every named existing regression command exits 0; the two dirty baseline files remain unmodified.\n\n## 2. What was wrong with S7 and S8\n\n### S7 — Discovery authority\n\nThe previous implementation added `detectionOwner: 'cortex'` and `detectionDisagreement` to the facts output. These are labels, not enforcement. `detect()` at `collect-facts.mjs:239` is still defined and still called at line 1284. `buildChecks(d)` derives every check from `detect()`'s output. No Cortex workspace roots, file classes, or ownership data reach the adapters.\n\n**Requirement:** `detect()` stops deciding provider applicability. Cortex workspace roots, file classes, language ownership, generated/vendored state, and exact file sets pass into legacy adapters. Internal detection disagreement produces a typed adapter error only.\n\n**Conformance case rewrite:** Case 6 must assert the *absence* of `detect()` from the applicability path — specifically that `buildChecks` does not use `d` to determine which checks run, and that Cortex projection data flows into the check execution context.\n\n### S8 — Verification exactness\n\nThe previous implementation made build/blocked exclusion explicit `UNPROVEN` and added a provider result digest log line. But there is no `resultDigest` field, no scope replay of `--type/--base/--base-commit/--dir`, and no artifact-digest comparison.\n\n**Requirement:** Replay uses the original type, base, base-commit, and dir options from the sealed plan. Comparison uses normalized result digests, finding IDs, locations, and artifact hashes. Any provider intentionally not replayed is reported UNPROVEN, never silently excluded.\n\n**Conformance case rewrite:** Case 7 must assert the *presence* of a digest comparison that produces a mismatch when evidence changes — not just that `verifyPlanSeal` is called.\n\n## 3. Scope & Ownership\n\n- **OWN — may edit:** `tools/skills/audit/collect-facts.mjs`, `tools/skills/audit/audit-verify.mjs`, `tools/skills/audit/tests/run-audit-conformance-tests.mjs`\n- **READ — read only:** `tools/skills/audit/adapters/cortex-projection.mjs`, `tools/skills/audit/audit-plan.mjs`, `tools/skills/audit/audit-complete.mjs`\n- **FORBIDDEN:** every file outside the three OWN paths; commit, push, network, dependency installs\n\n## 4. S7 — Remove detect() from the applicability path\n\n### Current state\n\n`collect-facts.mjs` line 239 defines `detect()` which returns a `d` object with `d.git`, `d.node`, `d.ts`, `d.py`, `d.rust`, etc. Line 1284 calls `const d = detect()`. `buildChecks(d)` uses `d` to determine which checks are applicable (e.g., `if (!d.ts) return { status: 'skipped' }`).\n\n### Required change\n\n1. `detect()` still exists for toolchain *presence* (so we know which commands to use), but it must NOT determine which checks are *selected* for execution.\n2. Check selection comes from the plan's `expectedChecks` (passed as `--only`). This already works — the `--only` filter selects which checks run.\n3. Within a selected check, if the toolchain is absent, the result is `unproven` (not `skipped`). This preserves the denominator.\n4. The `d` object must carry Cortex projection data (parsed extensions, source files, workspace roots) alongside the local detection. These come from the plan's scope options.\n5. Internal detection disagreement (local says absent, Cortex says present) produces a typed error in the check result, not a silent skip.\n\n### Implementation sketch\n\nIn `buildChecks(d)`, change every `if (!d.X) return { status: 'skipped' }` to `if (!d.X) return { status: 'unproven' }` for checks that are in the plan's expected set. The `d` object receives `cortexParsedExtensions` and `cortexSourceFiles` from the plan's scope.\n\n### Conformance case 6 rewrite\n\n```javascript\n// Case 6 must assert:\n// 1. buildChecks does not produce 'skipped' for checks in the expected set\n// 2. Cortex projection data (parsedExtensions) reaches the check context\n// 3. detectionDisagreement is a typed error, not a silent skip\nassert(!collectSource.includes(\"status: 'skipped'\") || !collectSource.includes(\"if (!d.\"), \n  'checks must not skip based on detect() when plan expects them');\nassert(collectSource.includes('cortexParsedExtensions') || collectSource.includes('parsedExtensions'),\n  'Cortex projection data reaches check context');\n```\n\n## 5. S8 — Add scope replay and artifact digest comparison\n\n### Current state\n\n`audit-verify.mjs` rebuilds the plan and compares provider set + contract digests. It re-runs deterministic checks and compares status + findings_count. But it does NOT:\n- Pass `--type/--base/--base-commit/--dir` from the sealed plan's scope\n- Compare result digests (only status + findings_count)\n- Compare artifact hashes (draft, evidence, claims)\n\n### Required change\n\n1. When re-running checks, pass the sealed plan's scope options (`--type`, `--base`, `--base-commit`, `--dir`) to `collect-facts.mjs`.\n2. After re-running checks, compute a SHA-256 over the normalized check results and compare with the prior run's digest.\n3. Compare artifact hashes: load the prior report's evidence.jsonl, claims.jsonl, draft.md hashes and compare with current state.\n4. Any provider in the plan that is NOT replayed (build, blocked, supplemental) is reported as `UNPROVEN` with its reason.\n\n### Implementation sketch\n\n```javascript\n// In audit-verify.mjs, after the check replay section:\n\n// 1. Scope replay\nconst scope = priorPlan.scope ?? {};\nconst scopeArgs = [];\nif (scope.type && scope.type !== 'all') scopeArgs.push('--type', scope.type);\nif (scope.base) scopeArgs.push('--base', scope.base);\nif (scope.baseCommit) scopeArgs.push('--base-commit', scope.baseCommit);\nif (scope.dir) scopeArgs.push('--dir', scope.dir);\n\n// 2. Result digest comparison\nconst resultDigest = (checks) => {\n  const normalized = checks.map(c => ({ check: c.check, status: c.status, findings_count: c.findings_count }));\n  return sha256(canonicalJson(normalized));\n};\nconst priorDigest = resultDigest(prior.checks ?? []);\nconst freshDigest = resultDigest(fresh.checks ?? []);\nif (priorDigest !== freshDigest) {\n  console.log(`DRIFT  result digest: expected=${priorDigest} observed=${freshDigest}`);\n  drift += 1;\n} else {\n  console.log(`MATCH  result digest ${priorDigest}`);\n}\n\n// 3. Artifact hash comparison\nfor (const name of ['draft', 'evidence', 'claims']) {\n  const path = join(dirname(factsPath), `${name === 'draft' ? 'draft.md' : name + '.jsonl'}`);\n  const priorHash = prior.artifact_hashes?.[name];\n  const currentHash = existsSync(path) ? sha256(readFileSync(path)) : sha256('');\n  if (priorHash && priorHash !== currentHash) {\n    console.log(`DRIFT  artifact ${name}: expected=${priorHash} observed=${currentHash}`);\n    drift += 1;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Conformance case 7 rewrite\n\n```javascript\n// Case 7 must assert:\n// 1. verifier passes scope options from sealed plan\n// 2. verifier compares result digests (not just status)\n// 3. verifier compares artifact hashes\nassert(verifySource.includes('--type') || verifySource.includes('scope.type'),\n  'verifier replays with sealed scope options');\nassert(verifySource.includes('resultDigest') || verifySource.includes('result_digest'),\n  'verifier compares result digests');\nassert(verifySource.includes('artifactHash') || verifySource.includes('artifact_hash'),\n  'verifier compares artifact hashes');\n```\n\n## 6. Verification\n\n| Requirement | Verification command | Expected result |\n|---|---|---|\n| S7: detect() not in applicability path | `rg -n \"status: 'skipped'\" tools/skills/audit/collect-facts.mjs` | Zero matches (all changed to `unproven`) |\n| S7: Cortex data reaches checks | `rg -n \"parsedExtensions\\|cortexFiles\" tools/skills/audit/collect-facts.mjs` | Present in check context |\n| S8: scope replay | `rg -n \"scope.type\\|scope.base\\|scope.dir\" tools/skills/audit/audit-verify.mjs` | Present in check invocation |\n| S8: result digest | `rg -n \"resultDigest\\|result_digest\" tools/skills/audit/audit-verify.mjs` | Present with SHA-256 comparison |\n| S8: artifact hash | `rg -n \"artifactHash\\|artifact_hash\\|draft.md\\|evidence.jsonl\\|claims.jsonl\" tools/skills/audit/audit-verify.mjs` | Present with comparison |\n| No regression | `AUDIT_PLAN_SIGNING_KEY=test AUDIT_OFFLINE=1 node tools/skills/audit/scripts/self-test.mjs` | 67/67 pass |\n| Conformance | `AUDIT_PLAN_SIGNING_KEY=test AUDIT_OFFLINE=1 node tools/skills/audit/tests/run-audit-conformance-tests.mjs` | 11/11 pass |\n\n## 7. Recovery\n\nIf S7 or S8 cannot be completed, preserve the partial diff and report which step failed with evidence. Never relax the conformance case to make it pass against a label.\n\n## NEXT\n\nOrchestrator reviews the diff, reruns verification, and decides on commit.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
