r validated receipt |\n\n## 1. Mission\n\n- **Outcome:** Nemesis preserves current architecture upgrades, restores two proven legacy regressions, clears 23 Windows failures, replaces every source-level mapped or blocked task with tested behavior, & pushes verified Nemesis `main`.\n- **Definition of done:** legacy inventory is 135 retained / 0 missing; Windows tests are 343/343 or higher; Books 1–8 source ledger has zero `mapped` & zero source blockers; external signing, native-binary, device, reviewer, publication, & model evidence stays explicitly unqualified; full Windows + macOS source gates pass; pushed `origin/main` equals local `HEAD`.\n- **Non-goals:** release build, signing, notarization, upload, package publication, paid provider execution, fabricated native/device/reviewer receipts, root-repository gitlink commit.\n\n## 1A. Decision & Experiment Question Lock\n\n- **Task semantics:** REPEATED_FAILURE\n- **Primary decision questions:** QUESTION_1: Does current source retain legacy behavior? QUESTION_2: Are all Books 1–8 source contracts implemented & truthfully qualified? QUESTION_3: Do Windows & macOS source gates pass from exact pushed bytes?\n- **Decision rule:** DECIDE_BY: legacy missing=0; source mapped=0; source blocked=0; Windows failures=0; macOS failures=0; external blockers non-green; origin/main equals HEAD.\n- **Acceptance metrics only:** METRICS_ONLY: legacy missing count; source mapped count; source blocker count; Windows failed tests; macOS failed source gates; origin divergence; baseline/final/origin SHA equality; critical open-claim count.\n- **Diagnostics only:** DIAGNOSTIC_ONLY: per-test duration, provider timing, coverage percentage, file-size inventory, & benchmark latency explain failures but never decide acceptance.\n- **Explicit forbidden scope:** FORBID: release quality claims | signing | notarization | upload | registry publication | live paid model calls | simulated human approval | root or sibling edits.\n- **Workload / fixture r